# Rapid Reload, WITH the feat. inc-l59x.
#
# Load the frozen Bard who has FT_RAPID_RELOAD (lib/FeatTab.cpp:1154) and an
# uncocked arbalest, put the arbalest in the Weapon Hand, and crank it once.
# The turn stamps of the @dump lines before and after the crank are what
# tools/check_rapid_reload.sh reads: the crank's cost is
# Creature::LoadCrossbow's `Timeout += N` (src/Item.cpp), made visible as the
# turns that pass before the game asks for the next key.
#
# The arbalest starts worn in the L. Shoulder slot, so `e SPACE` lifts it into
# the air and `b SPACE` sets it down in the Weapon Hand (the long sword comes
# out). The `s` before the dumps buys the one real turn a loaded session needs
# to count as gameplay rather than a stall (tools/headless.sh, inc-loa.3).

@dump:arrival
s
@dump:searched

i
e SPACE
b SPACE
@while "ESC:Done" ESC
@dump:wielded

f                       # fire: the uncocked crossbow is cranked instead
@dump:reloaded

@quit
